  "milestones": [
    {
      "key": "M1",
      "title": "Portable substrate",
      "description": "Outcome: the repository has an executable TypeScript toolchain and the same configuration, contract, filesystem, lock, process, and CLI guarantees are proven on current macOS, Windows, and Linux. Scope boundary: no scheduling policy, self-promotion, or consumer mutation. Exit evidence: trusted three-OS harness receipts plus the portable contract, capability, and primitive conformance matrices."
    },
    {
      "key": "M2",
      "title": "Minimum orchestration kernel",
      "description": "Outcome: one policy-neutral cycle can acquire a lease, select work through an adapter, dispatch a concrete worker, obtain independent review, journal the result, apply breaker and routing policy, and recover under supervision. Scope boundary: isolated fixtures only; no production bootstrap or consumer cutover. Exit evidence: a bounded end-to-end fixture cycle with crash, stale-authority, self-certification, and provider-boundary negatives."
    },
    {
      "key": "M3",
      "title": "Self-hosting release",
      "description": "Outcome: independently authorized bootstrap N0 uses the minimum kernel, concrete worker host, independent review, final OS certification, and promotion protocol to produce and activate N1. Scope boundary: no external-consumer authority transfer. Preparatory slices run whenever their native dependencies clear. Exit evidence: N0 bootstrap receipt, joined N0-to-N1 journal, exact-candidate review and promotion receipts, negative controls, and a healthy next routine N1 cycle."
    },
    {
      "key": "M4",
      "title": "Chase Sets integration-ready",
      "description": "Outcome: the Chase Sets adapter composition, authoritative parity fixture, and state-import recovery contract are ready to consume a self-hosted platform release. These slices may complete in parallel with kernel and self-host work when their native dependencies clear. Scope boundary: no live Chase Sets shadow or mutation. Exit evidence: adapter build, fixture coverage, and a disposable import/recovery rehearsal."
    },
    {
      "key": "M5",
      "title": "Chase Sets adoption",
      "description": "Outcome: Chase Sets pins the self-hosted platform release, proves authoritative shadow parity, and transfers orchestration control with tested recovery. Scope boundary: no second consumer or general marketplace. Exit evidence: terminal shadow report, cutover/recovery receipts, and the post-cutover observation report."
    }
  ],
